%% AS-IS returns flow — Vastra (annotated with measured delays)
%% Lanes: Customer | App | Courier | Warehouse QC | Refunds | CX
flowchart TB
    subgraph Customer
        C1[Customer requests return<br/>clicks reason code<br/>⚠ reason codes unreliable: 'damaged' 2x over-selected]
    end
    subgraph App["App / OMS (today)"]
        A1[Return logged<br/>NO fee logic<br/>NO exchange default]
        A2[Pickup request sent to courier<br/>⚠ no pickup SLA in contract]
    end
    subgraph Courier
        K1[Courier attempts pickup<br/>⚠ 10–18% need reattempts<br/>XpressBees 17.8% vs Delhivery 10.3%]
        K2[⚠ 30% of handoff scans missing<br/>no timestamp = no accountability]
        K3[Transit to warehouse<br/>avg 4.0 days]
    end
    subgraph QC["Warehouse QC"]
        Q1[Item received<br/>joins backlog]
        Q2[⚠ QC runs MONDAY BATCH<br/>avg wait 4.1 days<br/>standing backlog 1,500–2,300 units]
        Q3[Manual inspection<br/>result: resellable / damaged / defective]
    end
    subgraph Refunds
        R1[Refund initiated<br/>avg 2.0 days after QC]
        R2[Finance processes manually<br/>⚠ WH-Mumbai counts business days,<br/>WH-Delhi calendar days — SLA unmeasurable]
        R3[Refund credited<br/>total 9–14 days; 56.8% breach 14-day SLA]
    end
    subgraph CX
        X1[Customer asks 'where is my refund?'<br/>14.0 WISMO / 100 breached returns<br/>vs 4.4 clean — 3.2x]
        X2[Agent investigates manually<br/>5,180 hrs/yr on breached alone]
    end
    C1 --> A1 --> A2 --> K1 --> K2 --> K3 --> Q1 --> Q2 --> Q3 --> R1 --> R2 --> R3
    R3 -.->|breach| X1 --> X2
    K1 -.->|failed attempt| K1
